# codeloop lane: build (v1)

Run `codeloop card show <id>` first; the card says which stage it is in. Gates are approved only by a person.

| Stage | Skill | Output | Done check | Gate |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| research | research | {spec}/research.md | `codeloop check research {id} --min-sources 3` |  |
| interview | interview | {spec}/interview.md | `codeloop check questions {id} --min 3` |  |
| mock | mock |  | `codeloop check mock {id}` |  |
| spec | spec | {spec}/tasks.md | `codeloop spec check {id}` | spec (owner, after the check passes) |
| build | api |  | `codeloop task check {id} --all-done && scripts/verify-head.sh` |  |
| verify | verify | evidence/{nnn}/verify.md | `codeloop verify {id}` | local (owner, after the check passes) |
| review | review | evidence/{nnn}/review.md | `codeloop check file evidence/{nnn}/review.md --has 'verdict: approve'` | pr (reviewer, after the check passes) |
| staging | release | evidence/{nnn}/staging.md | `codeloop check file evidence/{nnn}/staging.md --has 'result: pass'` |  |
| live | release | evidence/{nnn}/prod.md | `codeloop check file evidence/{nnn}/prod.md --has 'result: pass'` | prod (owner, before the stage runs) |

## research

1. Run `codeloop card show <id>`. It prints the output path, the done check, the stage notes and any earlier rejection notes. Follow those over anything remembered.
2. Run `codeloop wiki inject --files <files you expect to touch>` and read every page it prints.
3. Do the work with the `research` skill (.claude/skills/research/SKILL.md).
4. Write the result to `{spec}/research.md`.
5. Run `codeloop card advance <id>`. It runs `codeloop check research {id} --min-sources 3`. If it exits 2, read the output, fix the work and run it again. Stop after 3 failures: the card parks as stuck for the owner.

